[2026-06-04T20:53:15.057Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_626","type":"reasoning","text":"**Using git status**\n\nI need to check the current status of my Git repository. The command `git status` can help with that! It's simple: it shows me the staged, unstaged, and untracked files, giving me a clear view of the project's state. It’s a handy tool to ensure everything is in order before I start making commits or further changes. I wonder, have I been diligent about checking it regularly? I need to make sure I keep on top of this!"}}
