[2026-06-04T21:05:04.309Z] [INFO]   ✅ Found pull request #16: "Add xpaste text capture across JS and Rust"
[2026-06-04T21:05:04.679Z] [STDOUT] Closes #15.

## Summary

- Added xpaste.pro URL normalization for canonical `/p/<id>`, `/p/<id>/raw`, `/ru/p/<id>`, and `/en/p/<id>` URLs in both JS and Rust.
- Added `/txt` support for normalized raw paste downloads and CLI `txt`/`text` capture support.
- Updated `/markdown` for xpaste URLs to capture the visual paste page in header/main/footer order, append the raw paste text as `xpaste-pro-<id>.txt` when the final Markdown is under 1500 lines, and return a ZIP with `index.md`, `xpaste-pro-<id>.md`, and `xpaste-pro-<id>.txt` for larger pastes.
- Added fixture-backed mock, unit, integration, and e2e tests under `js/tests/xpaste`, Rust xpaste unit/integration coverage, fixture regeneration helpers under `scripts/xpaste`, docs, a JS changeset, and a Rust version bump.

## Reproduction / Verification Paths

- `GET /txt?url=https://xpaste.pro/p/t4q0Lsp0` returns `xpaste-pro-t4q0Lsp0.txt` from the normalized raw endpoint.
- `GET /markdown?url=https://xpaste.pro/p/t4q0Lsp0` returns visual-page Markdown plus the raw paste text block while the final result is under 1500 lines.
- `GET /markdown?url=https://xpaste.pro/p/t4q0Lsp0/raw` normalizes back to the visual page for Markdown, while still fetching raw text for the attachment block.
- Large paste fixtures return a ZIP containing `index.md`, page Markdown, and raw `.txt` content.

## Screenshot Fixture

Full-page xpaste fixture screenshot used by the mock extraction tests:

![xpaste full-page screenshot](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/blob/issue-15-ba41292e60dd/tests/xpaste/data/t4q0Lsp0-screenshot.png?raw=true)

## Tests

- `cd js && npm run check` passed; ESLint reports existing warnings only.
- `cd js && npm test -- tests/xpaste --runInBand` passed.
- `cd js && npm test -- --runInBand --testPathIgnorePatterns tests/e2e/docker.test.js` passed: 39 suites passed, 2 skipped; Docker e2e was not run locally because Docker is not installed in this environment.
- `cd rust && cargo fmt --all -- --check` passed.
- `cd rust && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` passed.
- `cd rust && cargo test --all-features --verbose` passed.
- `cd rust && cargo test --doc --verbose` passed.
- `node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs` passed.
